<title>JAPAN: Nippon Mining raises indium price by 7,000 yen/kg.</title>
<headline>Nippon Mining raises indium price by 7,000 yen/kg.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Mining and Metals Co said it raised its selling price for indium ingot by 7,000 yen to 40,000 yen per kg for large orders and 45,000 yen per kg for small orders for 99.99 percent pure metal, effective with March 28 shipments.</p>
<p>The company cited supply tightness and rising prices overseas among the reasons for the price hike, which followed a 4,000 yen price increase on March 3.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
